{"parentUuid":"b0e47a12-08c2-4d4a-89f9-c263c30a55b7","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root/SimPO","sessionId":"6821caff-8cb6-4a84-bed9-ac55d7c78dbd","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"glistening-enchanting-church","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Hv3qCKFi19iq3EzpLKCfFm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"SimPO\" \"loss\" \"sigmoid\" \"beta\" \"gamma\" python implementation code\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Simple Preference Optimization (SimPO)\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/simple-preference-optimization-simpo\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py at main · princeton-nlp/SimPO\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO/blob/main/scripts/simpo_trainer.py\"},{\"title\":\"Align Phi3 with CPO-SimPO. Align your LLM with less memory and… | by Zain ul Abideen | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@zaiinn440/cpo-simpo-training-phi3-mini4k-instruct-with-cpo-simpo-de8c58b3ac32\"},{\"title\":\"Loss Functions in Python - Easy Implementation | DigitalOcean\",\"url\":\"https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/loss-functions-in-python\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - fe1ixxu/CPO_SIMPO: This repository contains the joint use of CPO and SimPO method for better reference-free preference learning methods.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/fe1ixxu/CPO_SIMPO\"},{\"title\":\"CPO Trainer\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/docs/trl/v0.11.2/en/cpo_trainer\"},{\"title\":\"Associated Software\",\"url\":\"https://vanderbei.princeton.edu/LPbook/src/\"},{\"title\":\"Simple Preference Optimization with Reference-Free Reward\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sebastianraschka_implementing-direct-preference-optimization-activity-7200478041586753536-arQ1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - princeton-nlp/SimPO: [NeurIPS 2024] SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO\"},{\"title\":\"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward Yu Meng1∗\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.14734\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing Loss or Cost Function in Python from scratch | by Tarique Akhtar | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://tariqueakhtar-39220.medium.com/implementing-loss-or-cost-function-in-python-from-scratch-a6906428092e\"}]\n\nI found several relevant search results about SimPO (Simple Preference Optimization) loss implementation with sigmoid, beta, and gamma parameters. Let me provide you with the key findings:\n\n## SimPO Loss Function\n\nSimPO is a reference-free, length-normalized preference optimization method that uses average log probabilities to compare candidate responses.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n\nThe CPO-SimPO loss is formulated as: $L_{CPO-SimPO}(\\pi_\\theta;U) = -E_{(x,y_w,y_l) \\sim \\mathcal{D}} \\Big[ \\log \\sigma \\Big( \\frac{\\beta}{|y_w|} \\log \\pi_{\\theta}(y_w | x) - \\frac{\\beta}{|y_l|} \\log \\pi_{\\theta}(y_l | x) - \\gamma \\Big)+ \\alpha \\log \\pi_\\theta(y_w| x)\\Big]$\n\nWhere:\n- β (beta) is a scaling hyperparameter\n- γ (gamma) is a target reward margin incorporated into the Bradley-Terry pairwise loss to help separate winning and losing responses\n- σ represents the sigmoid function\n- The loss uses length normalization (dividing by |y_w| and |y_l|)\n\n### Python Implementation Resources\n\nThe official SimPO implementation is available at princeton-nlp/SimPO on GitHub, which includes simpo_trainer.py that computes the SimPO loss.\n\nThe codebase is built upon the alignment-handbook repo, and training can be launched using: `ACCELERATE_LOG_LEVEL=info accelerate launch --config_file accelerate_configs/deepspeed_zero3.yaml scripts/run_simpo.py training_configs/llama-3-8b-instruct-simpo-v2.yaml`\n\n### Key Hyperparameters\n\nThe three main hyperparameters to focus on are learning_rate, beta, and gamma. simpo_gamma defaults to 0.5 and is the target reward margin for the SimPO loss.\n\nThe official GitHub repository at https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO contains the complete Python implementation with all the sigmoid, beta, and gamma components.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"002dd08d-60a6-45fc-aed7-3590d2962a4d","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:14:57.105Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"\"SimPO\" \"loss\" \"sigmoid\" \"beta\" \"gamma\" python implementation code","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_vrtx_01EkCvYV6Sr5t1hp6di8rYTM","content":[{"title":"Simple Preference Optimization (SimPO)","url":"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/simple-preference-optimization-simpo"}]},{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_vrtx_01Fc1StQDanRp8H1ct1LLJBM","content":[{"title":"SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py at main · princeton-nlp/SimPO","url":"https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO/blob/main/scripts/simpo_trainer.py"},{"title":"Align Phi3 with CPO-SimPO. Align your LLM with less memory and… | by Zain ul Abideen | Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@zaiinn440/cpo-simpo-training-phi3-mini4k-instruct-with-cpo-simpo-de8c58b3ac32"},{"title":"Loss Functions in Python - Easy Implementation | DigitalOcean","url":"https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/loss-functions-in-python"},{"title":"GitHub - fe1ixxu/CPO_SIMPO: This repository contains the joint use of CPO and SimPO method for better reference-free preference learning methods.","url":"https://github.com/fe1ixxu/CPO_SIMPO"},{"title":"CPO Trainer","url":"https://huggingface.co/docs/trl/v0.11.2/en/cpo_trainer"},{"title":"Associated Software","url":"https://vanderbei.princeton.edu/LPbook/src/"},{"title":"Simple Preference Optimization with Reference-Free Reward","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sebastianraschka_implementing-direct-preference-optimization-activity-7200478041586753536-arQ1"},{"title":"GitHub - princeton-nlp/SimPO: [NeurIPS 2024] SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward","url":"https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO"},{"title":"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward Yu Meng1∗","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.14734"},{"title":"Implementing Loss or Cost Function in Python from scratch | by Tarique Akhtar | Medium","url":"https://tariqueakhtar-39220.medium.com/implementing-loss-or-cost-function-in-python-from-scratch-a6906428092e"}]},"I found several relevant search results about SimPO (Simple Preference Optimization) loss implementation with sigmoid, beta, and gamma parameters. Let me provide you with the key findings:\n\n## SimPO Loss Function\n\nSimPO is a reference-free, length-normalized preference optimization method that uses average log probabilities to compare candidate responses.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n\nThe CPO-SimPO loss is formulated as: $L_{CPO-SimPO}(\\pi_\\theta;U) = -E_{(x,y_w,y_l) \\sim \\mathcal{D}} \\Big[ \\log \\sigma \\Big( \\frac{\\beta}{|y_w|} \\log \\pi_{\\theta}(y_w | x) - \\frac{\\beta}{|y_l|} \\log \\pi_{\\theta}(y_l | x) - \\gamma \\Big)+ \\alpha \\log \\pi_\\theta(y_w| x)\\Big]$\n\nWhere:\n- β (beta) is a scaling hyperparameter\n- γ (gamma) is a target reward margin incorporated into the Bradley-Terry pairwise loss to help separate winning and losing responses\n- σ represents the sigmoid function\n- The loss uses length normalization (dividing by |y_w| and |y_l|)\n\n### Python Implementation Resources\n\nThe official SimPO implementation is available at princeton-nlp/SimPO on GitHub, which includes simpo_trainer.py that computes the SimPO loss.\n\nThe codebase is built upon the alignment-handbook repo, and training can be launched using: `ACCELERATE_LOG_LEVEL=info accelerate launch --config_file accelerate_configs/deepspeed_zero3.yaml scripts/run_simpo.py training_configs/llama-3-8b-instruct-simpo-v2.yaml`\n\n### Key Hyperparameters\n\nThe three main hyperparameters to focus on are learning_rate, beta, and gamma. simpo_gamma defaults to 0.5 and is the target reward margin for the SimPO loss.\n\nThe official GitHub repository at https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO contains the complete Python implementation with all the sigmoid, beta, and gamma components."],"durationSeconds":22.170757806000008},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b0e47a12-08c2-4d4a-89f9-c263c30a55b7"}
